  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gender Justice and Social Inclusion Programme in Bangladesh- Discretionary Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The action will be led by the Gender Justice and Social Inclusion (GJSI) Team of Oxfam, with support from the PROTIC Team of the Climate Justice and Natural Resource Rights (CJNRR) programme and the Enterprise Development Programme (EDP) Team of the Economic Inclusion and Justice (EIJ) programme. Research lead from Monash University will be Manika Saha, PhD, Research Fellow from the Information Empowered Communities Lab, supported by her team members from Department of Human -Centered Computing at Monash University, Australia. Research goal and specific objectives of the action:  The broader goal of this project is to co -create cyber safety awareness and capability -building interventions for women digital entrepreneurs (WDE) and social influencers in Bangladesh. under three primary objectives, as follows:  - Creating people -centered cyber safety awareness and capability building amongst women digital entrepreneurs and social influencers in Bangladesh  - Engaging with policy stakeholders in decision -making within the ecosystem to influence for effective cyber safety interventions to scale up  Research questions 1) What are the current perceptions, practices, and experiences of women digital entrepreneurs (WDE) and social influencers regarding cyberbullying and cyber crimes in Bangladesh? 2) How can we design and develop strategies for effective cyber awareness and capacity building programs? 3) How can we influence effective cyber safety interventions among program and policy stakeholders and decision makers in Bangladesh for impactful and sustainable solutions</narrative>
  </description>
